  "question": {
    "html": "<p>P and S are two points on a gravitational equipotential surface around a planet. Q and R are two points on a different gravitational equipotential surface at a greater distance from the planet.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The greatest work done by the gravitational force is when moving a mass from</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">P to S.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Q to R.</li><li data-label=\"C\">R to P.</li><li data-label=\"D\">S to R.</li></ol>"
